# Without this, `COPY . .` in the builder stage copies the *host's*
# node_modules (Windows-native binaries, and pnpm's own `.modules.yaml` recording
# host-specific paths) directly on top of the Linux node_modules the `deps` stage
# just installed correctly. pnpm's own consistency check then refuses to run —
# `pnpm build` fails inside `runDepsStatusCheck` because the tree on disk no
# longer matches what the lockfile and store say it should be. Excluding these
# is what makes the two-stage COPY (deps' node_modules, then the rest of the
# source) actually produce the Linux-correct tree it was designed to.
node_modules
.next
.git
*.log
.env*.local
